# BL-546 EPIC — SLICE 3 (parked design; NOT executed by the acceptance runner).
# This is a .feature.draft: no *.feature glob or the runtime picks it up, so the up-front design is
# preserved without hard-failing the gate on unbuilt slices (specifier slice-scoping rule, BL-233).
# When a slice is built, MOVE its scenarios into specs/features/BL-546-prompt-engine-model-aware-prompt-composition.feature
# in that same parcel, with its step handlers.
#
# SLICE 2 (fragment registry, per-model adapters, content-hash fragment
# cache) is no longer parked here - BL-574 materialized it as its own
# ticket/feature file (specs/features/BL-574-prompt-engine-slice2-fragments-adapters.feature),
# trimming its two scenarios out of this draft in the same parcel per this
# ticket's own notes, so the design is not carried in two places (BL-441).

Feature: PromptEngine fragments, adapters, versioning, and inspection

  # SLICE 3 — versioning, validation, and inspect CLI.

  # BL-546 validation-rejects-invalid-09
  Scenario: validation rejects a compose result with volatile content before the stable chunk
    Given a compose request that would place volatile content before the stable chunk
    When PromptEngine validates the composed prompt
    Then validation fails with a stable-ordering error

  # BL-546 inspect-manifest-10
  Scenario: inspect mode exposes the composed prompt and fragment hash manifest
    Given PromptEngine has composed a system prompt for role "coder"
    When an operator requests prompt inspection for that role
    Then the inspection output includes the full composed prompt
    And a fragment hash manifest with no secret values
